<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  DRAFT — not yet applied to build-app.sh. See
  docs/architecture/hardened-runtime-entitlements.md for the rationale behind
  every entry (and every deliberately-omitted entry) below. This has not been
  verified against a real Developer ID signing identity or the notary
  service; treat it as a starting point for that verification, not as a
  finished artifact.

  This targets Developer ID + hardened runtime distribution, NOT the Mac App
  Store and NOT App Sandbox. Enabling App Sandbox is a separate, larger
  architectural decision (it would require reworking disk/log/config file
  access through security-scoped bookmarks and would restrict subprocess
  execution) and is intentionally out of scope here — see the doc above.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Explicitly false for release builds. Allowing task ports lets a debugger
    attach to the running process; Apple's notary service rejects it, and it
    should never be true in a distributed build. Included explicitly (rather
    than omitted) so a debug-entitlements variant can override it visibly
    instead of silently inheriting a default.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.get-task-allow</key>
  <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
